    dct:description "The mechanism has measurable consequences, but relevant natural experiments are scattered and rarely isolate the proposed cause. Existing data can test case studies, not the broad counterfactual." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare phenotypic and genomic change after isolated colonization by intact multi-species assemblages versus single or compositionally disrupted colonists, controlling time and environment. Support requires little change in intact-group colonizations and more change when biotic relations shift." ;
